{"uid":"4fc33e345f9f0068","name":"test_logout_clears_cookie_with_same_security_attributes_it_was_set_with","fullName":"tests.integration.test_login_logout_api#test_logout_clears_cookie_with_same_security_attributes_it_was_set_with","historyId":"f532f2bf13a35c3527451cf5d48ae66b","time":{"start":1795055452621,"stop":1795055453153,"duration":532},"description":"Regression test for a live production finding (2026-07-07, Release\n    Pro smoke test): logout's delete_cookie() call didn't repeat\n    httponly/secure/samesite, so it silently fell back to Starlette's\n    default (samesite=lax) instead of this project's SameSite=Strict\n    cookie policy. Functionally harmless -- browsers match a cookie for\n    deletion by name+domain+path, not by attributes -- but the clearing\n    Set-Cookie header should still honestly reflect the same policy the\n    cookie was issued under, not depend on an implicit framework default.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Regression test for a live production finding (2026-07-07, Release<br />\nPro smoke test): logout's delete_cookie() call didn't repeat<br />\nhttponly/secure/samesite, so it silently fell back to Starlette's<br />\ndefault (samesite=lax) instead of this project's SameSite=Strict<br />\ncookie policy. Functionally harmless -- browsers match a cookie for<br />\ndeletion by name+domain+path, not by attributes -- but the clearing<br />\nSet-Cookie header should still honestly reflect the same policy the<br />\ncookie was issued under, not depend on an implicit framework default.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1795055311331,"stop":1795055311332,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"caplog","time":{"start":1795055452